The '''Corellian Run''' was a [[super-hyperroute]] that ran throughout the various regions of [[the galaxy]], starting at the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] in the [[Core Worlds]] and ending at [[Naos system|Naos]] and [[Lamaredd]].<ref name="TFABG" /> The hyperroute also passed through the [[Hetzal system|Hetzal]] and [[Ab Dalis system|Ab Dalis]] [[Star system|systems]].<ref name="LotJ">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref>

==History==
Created [[25,000 BBY|25,000 years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the Corellian Run played a great role in making the [[Corellian system]] into an economic powerhouse. The route ran south-east from the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] in the [[Core Worlds]] and ending at [[Naos system|Naos]] and [[Lamaredd]]. Along its path, the Corellian Run intersected with the [[Hydian Way]] [[super-hyperroute]], touching planets in every region of [[the galaxy]], from the Core to the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]. As well as the [[Perlemian Trade Route]], the Corellian Run formed the border of an area known as [[the Slice]], which became the most populated and explored region of the [[galaxy]]. Spanning further out into the Outer Rim, parts of the Corellian Run crossed with other [[Hyperspace route|trade routes]] to form the [[Spice Triangle]], a series of lanes popular among [[smuggler]]s and free [[Merchant|traders]].<ref name="BMF 18" />

The [[freighter]] ''[[Legacy Run]]'' was traveling along<ref name="LotJ" /> the Corellian Run<ref name="Galaxy Map">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref> when it was destroyed in the [[Great Hyperspace Disaster]]. At the [[time]] of the disaster,<ref name="LotJ" /> in [[232 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> it was considered an old and well-established hyperlane, which was why [[Hedda Casset]], the [[captain]] of the ''Legacy Run'', was surprised to encounter an obstacle in the middle of the route, which should have been impossible. The obstacle was in fact a [[Nihil]] [[Stormship]] travelling a [[hyperspace]] [[Path]], unique routes available only to the [[pirate]]s. As the planet [[Ab Dalis]] was located further down the hyperlane, it was subjected to the [[First Emergence|first]] of the [[Emergences]], fallout of the Great Disaster, one [[Standard day|day]] later.<ref name="LotJ" />

